Aim

To generate test coverage reports using JaCoCo in Maven and analyze code coverage.

Theory (Short)

JaCoCo is a Java code coverage tool used to measure how much of the code is tested.
It integrates with Maven and Jenkins to generate coverage reports such as line coverage and method coverage.

Steps
Step 1: Create Maven Project
mvn archetype:generate

Enter:

GroupId: com.devops.lab
ArtifactId: lab14-jacoco
Packaging: jar
Archetype: maven-archetype-quickstart
Step 2: Add Calculator and Test Files

Add:

Calculator.java
CalculatorTest.java

(Same files as previous experiment)

Step 3: Update pom.xml

Add:

JUnit dependency
Maven Surefire plugin
JaCoCo plugin

(Use given pom.xml)

Step 4: Run Maven Test
mvn clean test
Step 5: Generate Coverage Report

Check folder:

target/site/jacoco/index.html

Open in browser.

Step 6: View Coverage

Coverage report shows:

Line Coverage
Method Coverage
Class Coverage
Percentage of tested code
Step 7: Jenkins Integration (Optional)

Add Jenkinsfile:

pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {

        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                git 'https://github.com/username/lab14.git'
            }
        }

        stage('Build & Test') {
            steps {
                bat 'mvn clean test'
            }
        }
    }

    post {
        always {
            junit '**/target/surefire-reports/*.xml'
        }
    }
}
